{% raw %}---
# Dependency review is free on public repositories. On private ones it needs
# GitHub Advanced Security; without that entitlement the action errors, so the
# job skips instead of failing the build (ADR-0008).
#
# "Free" is not the same as "enabled". Neither an organisation that has never
# applied its security features to repositories nor a fresh personal repository
# passes this job. Both fail with:
#
#   Dependency review is not supported on this repository. Please ensure that
#   Dependency graph is enabled
#
# The two cases need different fixes, and the message names neither:
#
#   * Organisation: there is no Dependency graph toggle anywhere in its
#     settings, and a public repository inside one has nothing to enable
#     locally - applying the organisation's Advanced Security features to **all
#     repositories** is the fix, because the dependency graph arrives with
#     Dependabot.
#   * Personal account: there is no organisation to set, and the graph is off
#     even on a **public** repository, so it has to be enabled for that
#     repository in its Code security settings, or with
#     `gh api -X PUT repos/<owner>/<repo>/vulnerability-alerts`.
#
# Verified in both cases: the same commit failed before the setting was applied
# and passed after, with no change to this file.
name: dependency-review

on:
  pull_request:

concurrency:
  group: dependency-review-${{ github.event.pull_request.number }}
  cancel-in-progress: true

permissions:
  contents: read # read the dependency manifests being changed

jobs:
  dependency-review:
    name: Review dependency changes
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    # Public repositories have the entitlement, but it still has to be switched
    # on (see the header); private ones must opt in here.
    if: ${{ !github.event.repository.private || vars.GHAS_ENABLED == 'true' }}
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@11d5960a326750d5838078e36cf38b85af677262 # v4
        with:
          persist-credentials: false

      - uses: actions/dependency-review-action@2031cfc080254a8a887f58cffee85186f0e49e48 # v4
        with:
          fail-on-severity: high
{% endraw -%}
